ame">Mikhail Artemyevich Muravyov</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Mikhail Muravyov was a Russian army officer and Left Socialist Revolutionary who commanded Red forces after the October Revolution.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-bakunin"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mikhail-bakunin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Mikhail Bakunin</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Mikhail Bakunin was a Russian revolutionary anarchist and political philosopher, among the most influential figures of anarchism.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-borisovich-of-tver"><span class="enc-name">Mikhail Borisovich of Tver</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Mikhail Borisovich was the last Grand Prince of Tver, from 1461 to 1485.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-ermolaevich"><span class="enc-name">Mikhail Ermolaevich</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Mikhail Ermolaevich was a prince of Great Perm, the Komi land on the upper Kama, in the 15th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-frunze"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mikhail-frunze.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Mikhail Frunze</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Mikhail Frunze was a Bolshevik revolutionary and Red Army commander.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-gorbachev"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mikhail-gorbachev.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Mikhail Gorbachev</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Mikhail Gorbachev (1931–2022) was the last leader of the Soviet Union, g